k led by 6.7 afterwards."}, {"turn": 22, "text": "C1 lost 15.0 points, lifting Black's lead from +11.2 to +26.2. The engine's choice was D6, in the open centre rather than the crowded bottom-left corner."}, {"turn": 34, "text": "D8 lost 27.5 points, the worst of GPT-6.1 Sol's game, and Black's lead jumped from +10.9 to +38.4. The engine wanted F8, which Black played next. The two sides had been trading heavy losses since move 29, and this was the one that left Black far ahead."}, {"turn": 45, "text": "With Black ahead by 37.6, E9 lost 34.8 points and the lead collapsed to +2.8. It was the worst move of the game, and it turned a lost-looking position for White back into a close one."}, {"turn": 54, "text": "White led by 2.2 after Black's A6 lost 4.3. GPT-6.1 Sol's C6 then lost 6.3 points and put Black ahead by 4.1, a lead that held to the end. The engine's choice was B5, which Black took on the next move."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Every script was a liberties/capture/region inspection of one move the player had already named (the `inspect` function and `current-position-liberties.js`), plus board display, a replay of the actual game to check the final board, and file notes via apply_patch. Nothing looped over empty points to score candidates or played continuations forward, so no move was chosen or ranked by code.", "stop": false}}